    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/4271964D5A23CB0A237D41AAC40830FA/jobs/83246": {
      "title": "Campus Security Officer PT",
      "description": "Campus Security Officer PT You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Campus Security Officer PT Hot Job Emory, VA 24327; Marion, VA 24354 Apply Overview Salary Range $20.00 Hourly Position Type Part Time Staff Job Shift Any Education Level High School Apply Description About this position: Emory & Henry University Campus Police Department is now accepting applications for the position of part-time Police or Campus Safety Officer for the Emory and Marion Campuses. This part-time position is a pooled position and will be utilized primarily for operational relief on a periodic basis. Qualifications About our ideal candidate: This position requires a Department of Criminal Justice Services (CSO) certification. The training to obtain this certification will be provided by our department. Candidates for this position must possess a high school degree or equivalent, be at least 21 years of age, and have a valid driver’s license. A background check/criminal history will be conducted. Experience in the law enforcement or security field is a plus. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/4271964D5A23CB0A237D41AAC40830FA/jobs/122899": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, PT, Neuromuscular/Neuroscience",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, PT, Neuromuscular/Neuroscience You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor, PT, Neuromuscular/Neuroscience Marion, VA 24354 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Education Level Post Graduate Degree Category Education Apply Description Job Location: Marion, VA Position Type: Full Time Faculty Education Level: Post Graduate Degree (DPT, at minimum) About this position: Emory & Henry University invites nominations and applications for an Open Rank Clinical or Tenure-Track (Assistant, Associate, or Full) Professor in our CAPTE accredited DPT program in our CAPTE accredited DPT program. This position is a full-time, 12-month appointment with a preferred start date of May 1, 2026 or earlier . The Department of Physical Therapy, housed within the School of Health Sciences, also includes programs in occupational therapy, physician assistant studies, nursing, exercise science, and clinical mental health counseling. The School of Health Sciences is located in Marion, VA, 20 miles northeast of the flagship campus in Emory, VA. The 15-acre Health Sciences Campus is designed to promote interprofessional education and faculty collaboration across the School's academic programs. The educational facilities include multiple classrooms and clinical skills labs, a technology enhanced cadaver lab, several research labs, an applied physiology lab, pediatrics lab, ADL lab, and a clinical simulation lab with both high fidelity manikins and standardized patient exam rooms. The Health Sciences Campus includes several community outreach programs including a Falls Prevention Center and the Mel Leaman Free Clinic at Emory & Henry University. These entities provide clinical and research opportunities for students and faculty. Primary Duties: Teaching Research Mentorship of DPT students Participation in Departmental, School, and University service activities Qualifications Qualifications of our ideal candidate: Physical therapist with expertise in the areas of neuromuscular physical therapy and neuroscience Preferred qualifications include a terminal doctoral degree or progress towards completion of a terminal degree (e.g., Ph.D., Ed.D, DSc) Applicants with a DPT degree as their highest degree will also be considered, but those applicants must have documented expertise in the areas of neuromuscular physical therapy Eligibility for Virginia physical therapy licensure, evidence of an established or developing scholarly agenda, and previous clinical experience Advanced clinical certifications (e.g. Neurologic Clinical Specialist) or completion of a clinical residency or fellowship and teaching experience in a CAPTE accredited program are preferred, but not required Faculty rank, tenure status, and salary will be commensurate with academic qualifications, teaching and research experience, and relevant clinical specialist certifications To apply, submit your: Cover Letter Updated CV with contact information for three professional references Unofficial transcripts from all attended institutions of higher education for all degree levels (official transcripts required upon hire) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Service Philosophy Research Statement summarizing scholarship Finalists may be asked to submit confidential letters of recommendation for their references Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Information about the University and the DPT Program can be found at www.emoryhenry.edu and www.emoryhenry.edu/academics/programs/graduate-programs/doctor-physical-therapy-program For more information, please contact: Eric Coley, PT Program Chair ecoley@emoryhenry.edu / 276-944-6146 (office) Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/4271964D5A23CB0A237D41AAC40830FA/jobs/170425": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Clinical Mental Health Counseling",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Clinical Mental Health Counseling You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor, Clinical Mental Health Counseling Marion, VA 24354 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Faculty Education Level Post Graduate Degree Category Education Apply Description Assistant Professor, Clinical Mental Health Counseling Tenure-Track | Remote Emory & Henry University | School of Health Sciences | Department of Clinical Mental Health Counseling Full-time | 12-month appointment | Anticipated start: July 1, 2027 Emory & Henry University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Clinical Mental Health Counseling . This remote faculty position includes limited on-campus responsibilities, including approximately three weeks annually for course intensives, commencement, and activities related to program accreditation. We seek a faculty member who will contribute to our CACREP-accredited M.S. in Clinical Mental Health Counseling , maintain an active scholarly agenda, engage meaningfully with students and colleagues in a virtual environment, and participate in university, professional, and community service. Responsibilities Teach graduate courses in Clinical Mental Health Counseling in an online format, with on-campus intensives. Advise and mentor master's students. Provide clinical supervision for practicum and internship students. Maintain an active research agenda with peer-reviewed publications and professional presentations. Participate as core faculty in program governance and accreditation activities. Contribute to department and university service and professional organizations. Support ongoing curriculum, program, and accreditation development. Maintain a strong virtual presence with students and colleagues. Rank, Term, and Start Date Rank: Assistant Professor, Tenure-Track Appointment: 12-month contract Location: Remote with limited on campus requirements Anticipated Start Date: July 2027 Application Materials Submit the following through the Emory & Henry University job opportunities portal: Cover letter addressing the qualifications and interests described above. Curriculum vitae. Teaching philosophy statement, including experience and approach to online teaching. Research agenda statement. Names and contact information for three professional references. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Official transcripts will be required upon hire. About the Program Emory & Henry University's CACREP-accredited M.S. in Clinical Mental Health Counseling is a 60-credit, 24-month online program preparing students for professional counseling practice and licensure. The program emphasizes humanistic values, evidence-based clinical practice, trauma-informed and culturally responsive counseling, and service to diverse communities. Students complete supervised practicum and internship experiences and prepare for practice across a range of clinical settings. Qualifications Required Qualifications Earned doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited program . ABD candidates may apply but must complete the doctorate by the contract start date. Eligible for or currently licensed as a Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC) or equivalent and able to maintain active licensure throughout employment. Demonstrated excellence or clear potential in graduate-level teaching, including online instruction. Established research agenda or demonstrated potential for scholarly productivity. Commitment to working effectively with diverse populations and fostering inclusive learning environments. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching in an online environment. Clinical and teaching expertise in counseling children and adolescents. Leadership or service experience in professional counseling organizations. Active clinical practice experience; supervision-only experience does not meet this preference. Commitment to trauma-informed principles and practices in counseling education. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
